# Rust Ownership

A guide to **ownership**, *borrowing* and `&mut`.

## Ownership rules

- Each value has an [owner](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/).
- Only one owner at a time
  - moved on assignment
  - dropped at scope end
    second para

1. First
2. Second

## Borrowing

References let you use a value
without taking it.

```rust
fn main() {
    let s = String::from("hi");
    println!("{}", &s);
}
```

> At any time, one mutable reference **or** many immutable ones.

| Kind | Many? |
|---|---|
| &T | yes ¦ ok |
| &mut T | no |

